00:36.440 --> 00:38.240
All right. Hello and welcome to Camel Finance.

00:38.340 --> 00:40.400
I'm your boy Camel and welcome to the week.

00:40.500 --> 00:41.440
Welcome to Monday.

00:41.760 --> 00:44.340
Bitcoin managed to close a weekly higher high candle.

00:44.520 --> 00:45.540
So that is good.

00:45.920 --> 00:50.420
And confidence is growing that we are indeed in a new cyclical bull market.

00:51.000 --> 00:54.020
Targeting perhaps as high as 300k in 2029.

00:54.280 --> 00:55.700
That would be pretty wild, wouldn't it?

00:55.700 --> 00:57.520
The story is not the same for gold, however.

00:57.700 --> 01:09.440
Gold just failed a daily cycle, which sets it up for a left translated weekly cycle and a decline into not only the weekly cycle, but the four year cycle low, a.k.a. the half cycle low in the eight year cycle.

01:09.840 --> 01:12.860
I made a good case back here that I didn't think the sentiment matched for this.

01:13.080 --> 01:14.680
And we had to respect a couple of breakouts.

01:14.800 --> 01:17.060
Had to try to play a daily cycle in case it was going to do this.

01:17.060 --> 01:29.000
But the market has spoken and we are now in intermediate decline with left translation on about week seven here, which puts an opportunity sometime late this year for allocation to the metals and the miners.

01:29.380 --> 01:32.280
So in the meantime, it should be a case of something like this.

01:32.360 --> 01:33.700
And then off we go, I hope.

01:33.700 --> 01:45.340
What's even more interesting to me is if we can continue to blow off in the stocks, that sinks up the four year lows with stocks and gold, which does make me wonder if this whole thing may turn out to be a head fake.

01:45.520 --> 01:47.000
And then this thing sinks up as well.

01:47.460 --> 01:48.700
I don't want to assume that for now.

01:48.780 --> 01:53.620
For now, I want to assume that Bitcoin is about to throw up some sort of higher low in that same sort of timing window and then go.

01:53.980 --> 01:56.500
And as frustrating as it might be right now, I know I'm certainly frustrated.

01:56.940 --> 02:00.040
Risk management is what keeps you in the game long enough to catch the big moves.

02:00.040 --> 02:06.760
So it looks like we got a bit more suffering in the short term, but hopefully we should soon be able to get behind a nice big turn.

02:07.240 --> 02:17.780
The more these lows look to come up to sink as well, the more I would be thinking we can use some of the price action in the likes of, say, the gold or stocks to start to reduce what we can expect from Bitcoin.

02:18.120 --> 02:20.640
Speaking of what we can expect from Bitcoin, I found this, right?

02:20.700 --> 02:22.880
Bitcoin on the left here and Nvidia here.

02:23.740 --> 02:26.820
680 odd K in no time in practically a straight line.

02:26.920 --> 02:28.280
Could we see something like this?

02:28.280 --> 02:29.980
I would argue probably not.

02:30.200 --> 02:33.300
Now, there is this short term fractal here, which again is Nvidia and Bitcoin.

02:33.580 --> 02:35.260
Is Bitcoin about to do something like this?

02:35.580 --> 02:36.080
Don't get me wrong.

02:36.140 --> 02:38.340
I'm here for it, but I don't think so.

02:38.420 --> 02:44.840
And the primary reason I say that, as with any data, if you torture the data hard enough, you will indeed get it to say anything.

02:45.260 --> 02:50.020
But when I just overlay these two charts, Nvidia in blue, Bitcoin in the candles, the divergence is clear.

02:50.020 --> 02:59.180
We've clearly been in four-year cycle decline for Bitcoin, and now we're attempting here to print the first true higher high, followed by a higher low pullback, and off we go.

02:59.480 --> 03:04.040
I'm sure this thing is probably using some sort of offset for Nvidia.

03:04.460 --> 03:12.600
But to me, the correlation is quite clear here, and it clearly broke during Bitcoin's four-year cycle because the four-year cycle is the driving force behind Bitcoin.

03:12.600 --> 03:15.660
The semiconductors, though, do seem to be ready for a new high.

03:16.080 --> 03:21.240
They have truly bottomed here, and therefore we should be able to get a continuation of upside for the semis.

03:21.580 --> 03:31.080
The mags is a similar story, and if semis and mags are going to run higher, to me, that gives me increased confidence that we'll continue to see something like this, that extreme right translation in the stock market.

03:31.500 --> 03:34.100
And notice how everyone is saying bond yields to the moon at the moment.

03:34.100 --> 03:39.180
But as we've been talking about for a long time on this channel, we're in the neighborhood to start to see tops come in for the cycles.

03:39.620 --> 03:44.360
The question then remains, do we just get some kind of shallow weekly cycle decline and then off to new higher highs?

03:44.580 --> 03:51.400
Or are we about to see the top here with the yields heading down into, note the window, okay, December to February?

03:51.780 --> 03:54.420
Lots of assets and their cycles are coming together.

03:54.600 --> 03:58.520
They're starting to sync up for that kind of December to February timeframe.

03:58.960 --> 04:03.140
When you get syncing of cycles, it's normally a very powerful indicator of what is to come.

04:03.140 --> 04:06.720
Keep in mind, yields topping like this means bonds about to rally.

04:06.900 --> 04:09.540
That makes sense from the TLT seven and a half year cycle.

04:09.900 --> 04:16.340
And if bonds are going to rally, as we've got gold heading for the lows, as we've got the stocks putting in a blow off top and then crashing down,

04:16.580 --> 04:20.460
we can kind of do that thing where we say, show me the charts and I'll tell you the news, right?

04:20.480 --> 04:24.900
We can deduce that in the coming months, there will be some kind of narrative.

04:25.200 --> 04:31.960
There'll be something that the average investor latches onto as an explanation behind these forces that are driving the cycles.

04:31.960 --> 04:37.200
But remember, as we often say, the cycles are in control and it's the narrative that comes after the cyclical price action.

04:37.320 --> 04:46.840
So we can say now, based on the cycles, sometime around probably November or December, there will be something most investors become extremely concerned with.

04:46.960 --> 04:48.240
So we'll see what happens from the stocks.

04:48.380 --> 04:49.280
I haven't checked the futures yet.

04:49.320 --> 04:49.840
We'll take a look.

04:50.260 --> 04:52.060
Seems like they're more or less holding up at the moment.

04:52.180 --> 04:55.000
The US 100 position, again, more or less holding up.

04:55.100 --> 04:57.800
We've had a good move off the lows, so a bit of digestion makes sense.

04:57.800 --> 05:01.280
But we're still relatively early in the daily cycles, so I think we can continue to push.

05:01.640 --> 05:03.540
Gold and silver have failed their daily cycle.

05:03.640 --> 05:04.020
Here we go.

05:04.160 --> 05:06.220
So this is now left translated in the weekly cycle.

05:06.360 --> 05:07.060
We don't need this anymore.

05:07.340 --> 05:09.900
And we are now in this process of intermediate decline.

05:10.100 --> 05:12.280
Probably copy and paste a couple of these across.

05:12.780 --> 05:14.460
Something like this, I should think.

05:14.780 --> 05:19.700
And I drew this for the members this morning and said this is probably going to be the bull market breakout level.

05:19.860 --> 05:24.840
OK, I would expect this to be the level at which price is contained beneath until we reset this cycle.

05:25.160 --> 05:26.160
And then it should be time to go.

05:26.160 --> 05:28.200
I don't think we need this yellow squiggle anymore.

05:28.300 --> 05:30.420
I think this is going to play out more from sort of here now.

05:30.720 --> 05:32.960
And we were saying the sentiment didn't seem to match back here.

05:33.040 --> 05:34.620
That's now been confirmed by the market.

05:34.840 --> 05:38.760
And the thing to watch out for is that sentiment should get extremely negative into these lows.

05:38.820 --> 05:40.260
And most people won't want to buy them.

05:40.640 --> 05:43.020
So in here, they were sort of saying, oh, I told you so.

05:43.120 --> 05:43.780
You missed the move.

05:43.860 --> 05:44.400
You missed the bottom.

05:44.560 --> 05:44.920
Blah, blah, blah.

05:45.000 --> 05:46.700
The boat's left without us, whatever it is.

05:46.820 --> 05:51.840
And then when we get down here, should we do something like this, which is the most probabilistic outcome now based on the cycles,

05:51.840 --> 05:58.440
we should therefore see sentiment reach an extremely bearish zone, similarly to what we've got on the TLT trade at the moment, right?

05:58.520 --> 06:00.580
TLT is extremely bearish sentiment-wise.

06:00.720 --> 06:05.640
It's just about to touch that 78 level as of today that we've been talking about, 78 to 80 for a bottom.

06:05.980 --> 06:10.920
And notice how the weekly cycle is getting ready to turn, as is the monthly with bullish oscillator divergence.

06:10.920 --> 06:14.040
So a lot of these cycles are syncing up, as I was saying earlier.

06:14.420 --> 06:21.400
Meanwhile, the leadership, such as semis and the mags, is continuing to push higher, which tells me the stock should be bullish for a little while longer.

06:21.800 --> 06:24.720
And then Bitcoin seems to be in some sort of daily cycle decline here.

06:25.060 --> 06:31.080
Once we've got a new daily cycle in and confirmed, we'll be able to affirm this count, because I'm a little bit suspect of this current count.

06:31.160 --> 06:32.740
I've shifted it around a few times.

06:33.020 --> 06:38.780
I'm not really happy with what I've got, but I'm more happy with this than I have been with the previous counts.

06:38.780 --> 06:40.880
So the symmetry seems to be here.

06:41.240 --> 06:46.940
And if we can't get a new high sort of imminently, then it's entirely possible this whole thing will have to get shrunk down a bit like this.

06:47.200 --> 06:51.540
And then again, we're still looking for a major pivot around the same time as all the other cycle lows.

06:51.640 --> 06:57.200
It's just with Bitcoin, I'm kind of working under the assumption that it might be a higher low here instead of a new lower low.

06:57.460 --> 07:02.260
But at the same time, given that gold just failed its cycle, gold is now perhaps showing us the way.

07:02.260 --> 07:06.820
And I would not at all be surprised if we end up having a new lower low in here.

07:06.900 --> 07:08.020
I don't want to call for it now.

07:08.020 --> 07:12.820
I want to be bullish because we've got the higher high and I want to be able to flip based on that higher high to bullish bias.

07:12.820 --> 07:18.600
Because if you don't and you just kind of dogmatically stick with a it's going to print a lower low type attitude,

07:18.600 --> 07:23.040
then that typically is how you can end up getting completely locked out of bull moves.

07:23.420 --> 07:24.320
So I don't want to do that.

07:24.320 --> 07:26.180
I want to be bullish here until proven otherwise.

07:26.420 --> 07:29.940
And if instead of forming as a higher low here, it does come down and sweep the lows.

07:30.080 --> 07:34.540
In hindsight, we'll be able to say, well, yeah, I think that makes sense based on how sentiment didn't really match and that kind of thing.

07:34.700 --> 07:40.020
But in either case, there is going to be a tradable low sometime towards the end of the year for all of these asset classes now.

07:40.540 --> 07:44.540
And apart from Bitcoin, I expect significant lows on the rest of the charts.

07:44.680 --> 07:46.820
Bitcoin, like I said, we're going to hope for a higher low here.

07:46.920 --> 07:49.080
But if we get a lower low, it doesn't really make any odds to us.

07:49.400 --> 07:51.200
People are asking me to cover oil, so we'll quickly do that.

07:51.200 --> 07:55.120
I think it's leaving behind a daily cycle low here and we'll probably get some more chop and consolidation.

07:55.500 --> 07:57.380
But the call is still for it to move down here somewhere.

07:57.960 --> 08:00.460
And again, notice the low timing, right?

08:00.480 --> 08:04.360
That puts oil also in sync with the rest of these asset classes.

08:04.880 --> 08:06.900
